# Trusted presence dongles.
#
# Format:  <name> <65-byte uncompressed P-256 public point, hex>
#
# A presence-signed tag names only a key id (the first 8 bytes of SHA-256 over
# the point). The key material is always read from this file, never from the
# tag, so a tag cannot introduce a key nobody vetted. Adding a dongle is a
# reviewable change in history like any other.
#
# Enrol with:
#   python3 tools/presence_git.py enroll --port <serial> --name <label>
#
# Empty on purpose: no dongle has been enrolled yet, so any tag claiming
# presence is rejected until someone deliberately adds one here.
